1
00:00:00,910 --> 00:00:05,116
Hi — I'm a solo Chinese builder, based in San Francisco,

2
00:00:05,136 --> 00:00:06,922
and this is sotto.

3
00:00:07,879 --> 00:00:12,027
Before sotto, a hackathon project of mine grew into web3 games

4
00:00:12,047 --> 00:00:15,389
that reached up to two million mainnet transactions a month.

5
00:00:15,669 --> 00:00:21,043
So I know what it takes to turn a hackathon build into something people use every day.

6
00:00:22,006 --> 00:00:24,888
Now I'm building payments for AI agents.

7
00:00:24,908 --> 00:00:27,768
Agents are starting to buy their own data and APIs,

8
00:00:27,788 --> 00:00:30,270
and today every one of those payments is public:

9
00:00:30,458 --> 00:00:33,963
what they bought, from whom, and for how much.

10
00:00:34,243 --> 00:00:37,817
And nothing caps what an agent can spend.

11
00:00:38,776 --> 00:00:41,658
sotto makes those payments confidential by default,

12
00:00:41,678 --> 00:00:44,161
bounded by a policy the owner sets,

13
00:00:44,233 --> 00:00:46,460
and auditable with viewing keys.

14
00:00:47,077 --> 00:00:50,779
The public sees that a payment happened, not what it was.

15
00:00:51,257 --> 00:00:57,141
The owner sees every receipt, and an auditor can check exact amounts from the chain.

16
00:00:58,104 --> 00:01:00,598
It works with what agents already use:

17
00:01:01,343 --> 00:01:07,239
x402, the Machine Payments Protocol, an MCP server and an Agent Skill.

18
00:01:07,833 --> 00:01:11,744
And it runs end to end on Solana, Tempo and Zcash —

19
00:01:11,908 --> 00:01:16,980
where it's already live on the new NU7 testnet upgrade.

20
00:01:18,085 --> 00:01:19,244
Why me?

21
00:01:19,954 --> 00:01:23,981
I've already taken a hackathon project to millions of mainnet transactions.

22
00:01:24,238 --> 00:01:30,274
And I ship fast: working solo with Claude Code, I built sotto in three weeks —

23
00:01:30,438 --> 00:01:35,614
the SDK, the MCP server, and a Rust Zcash service.

24
00:01:36,674 --> 00:01:37,729
Why now?

25
00:01:38,207 --> 00:01:41,600
Solana's confidential transfers came back to mainnet this June,

26
00:01:41,620 --> 00:01:43,789
and almost nobody uses them yet.

27
00:01:44,162 --> 00:01:46,255
Agents are just starting to pay for things.

28
00:01:46,275 --> 00:01:50,349
The rails are ready, and nobody has laid them for agents.

29
00:01:51,408 --> 00:01:55,853
I'm looking for the accelerator, and a first design partner whose agents buy data.

30
00:01:56,621 --> 00:02:01,460
sotto: confidential, not anonymous. Thank you.
